  "prefLabel": "Lab 306.07 Wrap up or Owner Controlled Insurance Policy (OCIP) Termination",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Lab 306.07 Wrap up or Owner Controlled Insurance Policy (OCIP) Termination.\n\n(a) A carrier shall provide all the required information to the department by completing and filing a “Notice of Termination for OCIP Coverage” form 6WC-wut (7/2015), contained in appendix II as soon as possible but no later than 10 calendar days after the date the wrap up or OCIP policy was terminated.\n\n(b) Failure of a carrier to file an accurately and fully completed “Notice of Termination for OCIP Coverage” form 6WC-wut (7/2015) contained in appendix II shall result in continuation of such coverage until a properly completed notice is filed with the department.\n\n(c) A notice of “Termination for OCIP Coverage” form 6WC-wut (7/2015) contained in appendix II shall be filed by the carrier to the department for each of the following circumstances:\n\n(1) When a project is completed;\n\n(2) When a general contractor is no longer working on a project; or\n\n(3) When a sub-contractor is no longer working on a project.\n\nSource. #11065, eff 4-1-16",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/lab300.html"
